  "category_cues": {
    "_comment": "Phrases that name a CATEGORY rather than a substance. 'any allergies' is a request for the whole allergy list; 'allergic to penicillin' is a question about one substance. Before this existed every list phrasing was bound in synonyms.csv to the single SNOMED marker 609328004 'Allergic disposition (finding)', so a patient with nine allergy facts including penicillin answered 'any allergies' with one generic line that rendered as a complete, low-criticality section. An entity built from a cue here carries a category and NO codes, which makes retrieve() pass codes=None and get_patient_facts() return the whole category -- which is also what finally engages its never-top-k rule for ALLERGY.",
    "_precedence_comment": "A cue is dropped when the same query also resolved a specific entity in that category: 'any frusemide in the medication list' means frusemide, not the whole list. That is a deterministic post-parse rule over what already resolved, not an intent classifier -- nothing here inspects the query to guess what the clinician wanted.",
    "ALLERGY": [
